<h1>From N Points</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformations &gt; From N Points</b></span>.</p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Transformation From N Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command</span> creates a transformation constructed from a set of known points. The name of the entity is ‘System from points N’, where N is the number of the subsequent newly created datum alignment.</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="Images/N_Points_dialog.gif" width="465px" height="433px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:normal;">Use the two drop down lists to enter corresponding datum points or point reducible entities.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Add</b></span> button – add the point pair.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Remove</b></span> button – remove the point pair.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformation matrix</b></span> – the matrix that transforms points from one transformation to the other.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformation RMS</b></span> – indicates the error of the mapping between the two sets of points.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Bullet"><span style="font-weight:normal;">The sequence to create transformation is as follows:</span></p>
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:40px;">1. From the left hand list select a source point.</p>
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:40px;">2. <span style="font-weight:normal;">From the right hand list select the corresponding target point.</span></p>
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:40px;">3. Press Add button to add the pair of points.</p>
<ul type="disc" class="whs6">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">In case of error, i.e. a pair does not contain corresponding points – select this pair from the list of added pairs and press Remove button to remove it.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">After the third pair a matrix of transformation and RMS error is displayed.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:40px;">4. Repeat steps 1 – 3 to add all pairs of points.</p>
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:40px;">5. Press OK button to create the transformation.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Transformation schematic</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP289779721" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Images/image076.gif" width="750px" height="393px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: You have to add at least three pairs of corresponding points in order to generate transformation.</p>
<p class="Use" style="font-weight:normal;">Generate Co-ordinate System From N points method is <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>used</b></span> when aligning two separate data sets – sphere-to-sphere alignment and point-to-point alignment.</p>
